    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look primed for a high-ceiling performance today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29), who earns the top spot in our lineup. Facing Ryan Johnson, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite 5.15 xERA matchup and a massive 14% platoon edge, making him our primary engine for counting stats. **Kyle Tucker** (76.70) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) also anchor the outfield with strong projections; **Kyle Tucker** leverages the favorable matchup against Kendry Rojas, while **Jackson Merrill** is positioned to capitalize on a weak 5.06 xERA arm, despite a minor suppression risk due to the opposing catcher's efficiency at controlling the base paths. **Andy Pages** (74.01) rounds out our elite tier, offering excellent park factors and a strong matchup profile to keep the pressure on the opposition.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision was opting to sit **Josh Jung** (55.98) in favor of the higher-upside start from **Coby Mayo** (56.48). While **Josh Jung** maintains a respectable profile, the optimizer favored **Coby Mayo** due to the significantly softer matchup against Ryan Johnson compared to the tougher task of facing Sandy Alcantara. Elsewhere, we are exercising caution with **Drake Baldwin** (56.98) and **Wade Meckler** (52.44); both remain in the starting lineup to maximize our total game caps, but they represent our lowest projected efficiency scores and remain on a short leash should official lineups indicate a disadvantageous shift in batting order.\n\nInvestors should note that today\u2019s projections are based on assumed batting orders due to \"Lineup Pending\" status across the league. While players like **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (70.08) and **Jacob Wilson** (69.39) offer strong value today\u2014the latter bolstered by a 5% wind-out boost\u2014the reliance on these projected spots introduces marginal volatility. We have intentionally benched **Nasim Nunez** (41.45) despite his elite speed profile, as his projected #9 spot in the order and the presence of a sub-3.50 xERA opponent make him a liability for today\u2019s efficiency targets. We remain focused on leveraging the platoon edges for **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jackson Merrill** to maintain our competitive advantage in the 5x5 landscape.",
